@title secretshare14 — one source gate c ^= a | !b on secret-shared values
@subtitle The replicated per-gate body only: one SG (7-variant menu, sizes 4..6) + rg_freq=2 refresh gadgets (RG1/RG2 = 6, RG3 = 2).  Cost is a seeded draw: E = 36/7 + 2·14/3 ≈ 14.5 — the '14' in the name; seed 14 was chosen so this instance draws the average (6 + 6 + 2 = 14).  Share setup (cleartext→2-shared) and unshare (decoding) are fixed infrastructure, not part of the gadget.
@equation c' = c ⊕ (a ∨ ¬b),  with v = v_s ⊕ v_p for v ∈ {a, b, c}
@wire a_s a
@wire a_p a
@wire b_s b
@wire b_p b
@wire c_s c
@wire c_p c
@note c_s carriers re-pair after RG1/RG2 refreshes (labels are initial roles)
# SG — shared-gate variant 5 (menu of 7)
c_s <--- b_s | !a_s
c_s <--- b_s | !a_p
c_s <--- b_p | !a_s
c_s <--- b_p | !a_p
c_s <--- !b_s & b_p
c_s <--- b_s | !b_p
# refresh 1 of 2: RG1 re-share (0,1)
a_p <--- b_s | !b_p
a_s <--- b_p | !b_s
b_s <--- a_s | !a_p
b_p <--- a_p | !a_s
a_s <--- b_p | !b_s
a_p <--- b_s | !b_p
# refresh 2 of 2: RG3 re-share value 1
a_s <--- c_p | !b_s
a_p <--- c_p | !b_s
